      "writtenOn": "2024-05-24T20:22:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Something to resolve in a follow up CL.\n\nIf we want to commit this upstream eventually, the use of these wrappers won\u0027t be accepted upstream.\n\nAs is, the PPM implementation is a Zephyr application first, and linux userspace application second.\n\nI see 2 alternatives to the approach creating `platform_*` routines.\n\n1. Have the PPM implementation make Zephyr API calls directly.  The Linux userspace then needs to provide a translation fro the Zephyr APIs to the pthread APIs.\n\n2. Convert the PPM implementation to only use posix calls. \n\nFor option 2, Zephyr probably still wouldn\u0027t accept the PPM directly in tree.  But we could consider making it an optional Zephyr module.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 67,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "f2fbe5e70975a040ef0fa21fd2bc06fa8752218d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
